translatedData.subTitle:
Main text: Lately, the crypto market has been especially frustrating. Bitcoin has kept oscillating back and forth within a tight range of 64,000–65,500. It can’t climb higher, and it hasn’t fallen deeply either, leaving many people in agony holding their coins.
Over the past 24 hours, things have overall been experiencing a slight pullback. During the day, price briefly dipped to around 63,700, but was then pulled back above 64,000 by buy pressure. Trading volume has noticeably shrunk compared with the past few weeks, suggesting that neither bulls nor bears are willing to make big moves right now.

Why has it been moving sideways for so long:
First, the inflow of funds into spot ETFs has been intermittent rather than explosive, with no large-scale surge of new capital;
Second, the U.S. regulatory bill has been postponed again, with no clear positive catalyst in place, so big money doesn’t dare to push aggressively;

